Chrome suspends inactive service workers after ~5 minutes. Hamburg lacks a keep-alive mechanism.

## Source
djyde/browser-mcp implements keep-alive pings to prevent suspension.

## Problem
- If no tab interaction occurs for ~5 minutes, Chrome suspends the service worker
- This kills the WebSocket connection
- Next MCP call fails until user interacts with browser
- Hamburg has reconnect logic, but reconnect only triggers when an event handler runs (which won't happen while suspended)

## Solution
Add periodic ping in DriveSocket to keep service worker alive:

```typescript
// In packages/extension/src/background.ts
private keepAliveTimer: number | null = null;

// In DriveSocket.connect(), after socket opens:
this.keepAliveTimer = self.setInterval(() => {
  if (this.socket?.readyState === WebSocket.OPEN) {
    this.sendEvent("drive.keepalive", {});
  }
}, 30000); // Every 30 seconds

// In stop():
if (this.keepAliveTimer !== null) {
  clearInterval(this.keepAliveTimer);
  this.keepAliveTimer = null;
}
```

## Core Handler
Core should handle `drive.keepalive` as a no-op (just ACK).

## Risk if Not Fixed
WebSocket dies after idle periods, MCP calls fail silently.

## Effort
~30 minutes

Add ability to search browser history. Useful for research tasks where the agent needs to recall previously visited pages.

## Tool Definition
```typescript
{
  name: "browser.history_search",
  input: {
    query: string,        // Free-text search query
    max_results?: number, // Default 100
    days_back?: number    // Default 30
  },
  output: {
    items: Array<{
      id: string,
      url: string,
      title?: string,
      lastVisitTime: string,  // ISO timestamp
      visitCount?: number
    }>
  }
}
```

## Implementation Notes

### Permission Model
- Requires `history` permission in extension manifest
- Should be an **optional permission** - not requested by default
- Add UI toggle in extension popup for user to grant/revoke

### Extension Side
```typescript
// In CallHandler
async historySearch(params: { query: string; maxResults?: number; daysBack?: number }) {
  const hasPermission = await browser.permissions.contains({ permissions: ["history"] });
  if (!hasPermission) {
    throw new Error("History permission not granted");
  }

  const daysBack = params.daysBack ?? 30;
  const startTime = Date.now() - (daysBack * 24 * 60 * 60 * 1000);

  return browser.history.search({
    text: params.query,
    startTime,
    maxResults: params.maxResults ?? 100
  });
}
```

### Manifest Changes
```json
{
  "optional_permissions": ["history"]
}
```

## Privacy Considerations
- History contains sensitive browsing data
- Must be opt-in (optional permission)
- Consider adding a warning in tool description
- Never enable by default

## Use Cases
- Research recall: "Find that article I read about X"
- Context gathering: "What pages have I visited about Y?"
- Session recovery: "What was I working on yesterday?"

## Reference
- browser-mcp implementation: /Users/btraut/Downloads/browser-mcp-main/extension/calls.ts
- Comparison report: .context/browser-mcp-comparison.md

Capture screenshots beyond the visible viewport using DevTools Protocol.

## Why
Essential for long pages - currently only captures visible viewport via captureVisibleTab.

## YetiBrowser Reference
File: /Users/btraut/Downloads/yetibrowser-mcp-main/extensions/shared/src/background/index.ts
- Function: takeScreenshot (search for 'captureScreenshot')
- Uses Emulation.setDeviceMetricsOverride to expand viewport
- Falls back to captureVisibleTab for restricted pages

## Implementation

### 1. Schema Update (packages/shared/src/schemas.ts)
```typescript
const ScreenshotInputSchema = z.object({
  target: z.enum(['viewport', 'full']).optional().default('viewport'),
  fullPage: z.boolean().optional().default(false), // alias for target='full'
  format: z.enum(['png', 'jpeg', 'webp']).optional().default('png'),
  quality: z.number().min(0).max(100).optional() // for jpeg/webp
});
```

### 2. Extension Background (packages/extension/src/background.ts)
Add full-page capture using debugger:

```typescript
async function captureFullPage(tabId: number): Promise<string> {
  const target = { tabId };
  await chrome.debugger.attach(target, '1.3');

  try {
    // Get page dimensions
    const { result } = await chrome.debugger.sendCommand(target, 'Runtime.evaluate', {
      expression: 'JSON.stringify({ width: document.documentElement.scrollWidth, height: document.documentElement.scrollHeight })'
    });
    const { width, height } = JSON.parse(result.value);

    // Override viewport to full page size
    await chrome.debugger.sendCommand(target, 'Emulation.setDeviceMetricsOverride', {
      width: Math.min(width, 1280), // cap width
      height,
      deviceScaleFactor: 1,
      mobile: false
    });

    // Capture
    const screenshot = await chrome.debugger.sendCommand(target, 'Page.captureScreenshot', {
      format: 'png',
      captureBeyondViewport: true
    });

    // Reset viewport
    await chrome.debugger.sendCommand(target, 'Emulation.clearDeviceMetricsOverride');

    return screenshot.data; // base64
  } finally {
    await chrome.debugger.detach(target);
  }
}
```

### 3. Route Update (packages/core/src/routes/artifacts.ts)
- Check fullPage/target option
- If full, use debugger-based capture
- Fallback to captureVisibleTab on error

### 4. MCP + CLI
- Update tool schema to include fullPage option
- Update CLI to accept --full-page flag

## Edge Cases
- Fall back to viewport capture if debugger attach fails (restricted pages)
- Cap width at 1280px to avoid memory issues
- Handle very tall pages (maybe cap at 10000px height)

Handle alert(), confirm(), and prompt() dialogs via DevTools Protocol.

## Why
Pages with confirmation dialogs block automation. Essential for pages that use native JS dialogs.

## YetiBrowser Reference
File: /Users/btraut/Downloads/yetibrowser-mcp-main/extensions/shared/src/background/index.ts
- Uses Page.handleJavaScriptDialog via debugger
- Supports accept/dismiss
- Supports promptText for prompt() dialogs

## Implementation

### 1. Schema (packages/shared/src/schemas.ts)
```typescript
