Add explicit hover action that dispatches mouse events without clicking.

## Why
Reveals tooltips, dropdown menus, and hover states before deciding to click. Currently requires JS evaluation workaround.

## YetiBrowser Reference
File: /Users/btraut/Downloads/yetibrowser-mcp-main/extensions/shared/src/background/index.ts
- Dispatches: mouseover, mousemove, mouseenter events
- Returns snapshot after hover

## Implementation

### 1. Schema (packages/shared/src/schemas.ts)
```typescript
const HoverInputSchema = z.object({
  locator: LocatorSchema, // existing locator type (testid, css, text, role)
  tab_id: z.number().optional()
});
```

### 2. Content Script (packages/extension/src/content.ts)
```typescript
function hoverElement(element: Element) {
  const rect = element.getBoundingClientRect();
  const centerX = rect.left + rect.width / 2;
  const centerY = rect.top + rect.height / 2;

  const eventInit = {
    bubbles: true,
    cancelable: true,
    view: window,
    clientX: centerX,
    clientY: centerY
  };

  element.dispatchEvent(new MouseEvent('mouseover', eventInit));
  element.dispatchEvent(new MouseEvent('mouseenter', { ...eventInit, bubbles: false }));
  element.dispatchEvent(new MouseEvent('mousemove', eventInit));
}
```

